David Damerell wrote:

> As I keep pointing out, it does not make the vast majority of games _any_
> harder before the Castle. It just eliminates the outlying case where you
> get an enormously easier start.

Furthermore, and I think people seem to be ignoring this point, if you were
to simply make wands of wishing unrechargeable, they'd *still* be an
enormous boon in the early game -- you're still guaranteed a *minimum* of
two wishes.

If I had my druthers, I'd make this change, and also make it possible to
wish for magic lamps.  I think that the latter also has potential for
creating interesting decisions upon receiving one-time wishes from thrones,
fountains etc., e.g. "I'm not sure what I need right now, so should I go
for the lamp with an 80% chance of getting a wish later, or should I go for
a different guaranteed item right away?"

